    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0258" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.290/2–2751: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consulate General
                        at Lahore </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-02-27T14:00:00-05:00">February 27,
                            1951—2 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. For Gay. Re Chi representation, London reports indicate little prospect any
                    procedural formula can be worked out for which UK cld cast affirmative vote or
                    even abstention. Re nature Chi representation proposal ECAFE, Dept leaves ur
                    discretion in light current negotiating situation whether propose postponement
                    motion or support reaffirmation last year’s decision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
